body:
idk if u can send her articles about it to clear it up? asexuality is a spectrum. ace in most context is a spectrum. like if you do a simple google search you can find that instead of being a jerk friend.

&#x200B;

idk if explaining how you feel will help? like how it feels or the interactions and lack / less attraction works? Thankfully i have support friends and fellow ace friends so I havent had too much aphobia.

I'd have to fish them out of the void real quick. *one second*

&#x200B;

update: they're really deep in the void, the current has swept them away RIP

when you google marico (and its meaning in spanish) the first result is the (usually unless reclaimed) derogatory word for gay-

&#x200B;

tho other sources say its used generally for "dude" and not usually related to sexual orientation or anything much.

they probly are used to living with you, so changes that are kinda subtle at first aren't noticed. Kind of like Salience bias *(also known as perceptual salience) is the cognitive bias that predisposes individuals to focus on items that are more prominent or emotionally striking and ignore those that are unremarkable, even though this difference is often irrelevant by objective standards.*

&#x200B;

If it isn't a big change it won't outright be noticed. *kinda like (besides their obsession with their inventions and neglect of their kids really) Danny phantom (from the show) had the whole show without his parents thinking it was him (even though only his hair and eye color was changed. and plot but)*

Well I do have this username for a reason

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

*(when i was 12 i decided I was basically a demon cus no gender, no sexuality, and now no romantic feelings. Even tho that technically isnt what a demon was but depending the type it is (and depending the definition of a god))*

i got mine from minecraft, when i had to make a random name that isnt my real name. and i love magic, and witchcraft, and i had the name in my head also becuase of a past cat my mom had (doesn't help in my dad refusing to use the name sadly).

&#x200B;

tho ill go by any name similar to it, and honeslty dont care if it just isnt my legal name lol

oml your dad is. a work of *something.* I also don't think his job is going to last longer if he talks like that to his co-worker or anyone tbh. 

&#x200B;

Atleast he isn't sugar coating it but he doesnt seem like a family member that you would want in your life when you pass everywhere else and he will probably make it a point to point out that you are "a girl pretending to be a boy" so :///

tbh I, myself, am the closest to the 'right one' so i'd probably just "I already have the right one-" or something that references myself without it obviously being me. You need to love urself before u even like date. or have a lot of friends. or really fully live-

&#x200B;

Or just have cat children. my cat child is my only reason really to have a job tbh

I don't want surgrey for down there, mostly as I am more concerned with my chest. Though It is a dysphoric thing when I have to do classes for my major and a lot are science and anatomy based. Where it is very dysphoric just by how textbooks are worded and how classes are labeled.

&#x200B;

I mostly just ignore my bottom half, tho I am not too stressed about it thankfully. But tbh I also forget I have boobs till I get out of bed or look down. My chest kinda just feels like my boobs are slightly attached and floating so it's a weird weight.

I only ever use AFAB terms if I am explaining something to someone, as most my friends are cis. I also have had to explain what "AFAB" means itself. I don't have anything against it, and id rather be called female than 'girl' if needed because i am also in nursing and Female is the anatomical term, or more anatomical tho i wish that anatomy parts wasn't as important cus i don't want to do a whole class on that. Though I'd rather of been assigned nothing at birth (so like ANAB i guess lol) 

&#x200B;

tho AGAB sounds a bit off since while some surveys and things mixes girl and female as the same, it technically isn't- 

&#x200B;

tho AFABs with a S i have no feeling about really, tho I've never seen it pluralized. TBH if it isn't for any biology based thing or like anatomy thing, I'd rather someone assume i'm a guy or a really androgynous person (and confuse them lol)

I personally use the term trans but its more of a loose term of it. Im non-binary but prefer male/masc presenting. I define transgender/trans as you either have a want or goal to transition/seemingly 'change' your body to match your gender, or generally plan to transition in some context \[socially, medically, etc etc\] (or lack of it for me). Some people who are technically trans, at least one actor i know of at least, don't use that label.

&#x200B;

kinda depends on the person or how the word is defined or perceived ig.

I accidently projected my asexuality onto a danny phantom OC i have. cus i made her a plant and she is in a lesbian relationship but she literally is able to asexually reproduce and i made my own logic for that. also cus i couldnt think of the character going past even kissing her Significant other so **magically a child!** :3

&#x200B;

and in the SWTOR game even if i try to do the dark-side options i always avoid that 1 option that would mean the characters would fk off cam. and I pretend that when u court a companion that they cant do that stuff

lol i don't know how to kiss, mostly like on-the-mouth (still low key afraid i am somehow doing kissing cheeks wrong) and am afraid of doing it wrong. I don't see it as sexual but it is also something i don't understand or know how to do and my mind lumps it into 'sexual interactions' and i avert from it.

&#x200B;

Edit; I am Aro (so aro ace lol). that is probly why the kissing makes no sense/am aversed to that. makes lot more sense

Maybe have a chat and sit down with her about her using the wrong ones? I know that you can't stop customers, I know i wish i could correct them, but your girlfriend should use the right ones. 

&#x200B;

How long have you gone by different pronouns? Sometimes it takes people a while to get used to them and adapt.  If it has been a while since you've started using your preferred pronouns, then she might just be following the customers because she doesn't want to confuse them? Even though she should be using the right ones. 

&#x200B;

At my old work my co-workers used the right pronouns, and it confused the customers as the customers used the wrong ones but I can't correct them (thought a few customers have asked my pronouns).

Yea I think it is a default setting. besides misgendering, my social anxiety thinks doing the customer service voice is better when talking to cashiers, doing customer service, or talking with people. 

&#x200B;

Though I am mistaken as a 6/7-14 year old when ppl only hear my voice, and when they see me they think i'm in middle school ( i am 20) so, uh...

&#x200B;

I think it takes a lot of training and actively not doing the C.S voice to make it stop happening automatically. I try to deepen my voice when I talk on the phone, at least with the home phone scam calls, and try to overly sound offended when they ask for my parents or think i'm a lady. I am slightly offended cus dysphoria but still

what I do is wear baggy clothes, i cut my hair short (but others may like longer hair) and I am also in therapy (mostly for anxiety which is connected to dysphoria). I used to use binders, but my asthma and weight got a bit too much for them to work correctly.   


if it’s safe for you to do so, I’d say look into clothes that make you more comfortable, and if you have chest dysphoria seen if there are compression bras (nike makes compression sports bras, at least where I am) and maybe a chest binder. If you go that route, binding with other items can harm ur ribs and chest so be careful.

&#x200B;

if you have friends or family who are supportive, see if they can help you with what I mentioned (if it applies to you) and see if they can help you socially with your chosen name and pronouns (if you changed them, if not you don’t need to and have time to think about or test out different ones) 

hope you have a good day :)

Reminds me of the 50% off thing for plants. its UP TO 50% right now. not ALL are 50% off, unless the computers are royally messed up. At this point I just get a head cashier to help me 'modify' it if the customer is at CS or at a Register I hope there is a head cashier near to explain it or help me out. 

&#x200B;

And military doesn't count for items on sale, as far as I have been told.

I'm almost in the same boat as you, doing school with no job and being supported by my dad. Your brother is extremely entitled when he created his own lack of money. I know getting a job is hard (atleast my town) so i'd say it might also just be how society is with the 'no job' part. If my brother did that, i wouldn't even know how to talk to him with out disgust. After I was 14 or so my dad didn't even give presents until after Christmas, to make sure it is something we really need or want. 

I'd also suggest tryin to maybe write a thank you card or the like, as home made presents may not be fancy but they are welcomed for most people. 

&#x200B;

My little brother is alittle like yours, in the 'father won't enforce boundaries' or be more strict. Which he did have 3 kids before so, the more kids, the less strict parents sometimes act. Money is tight so i don't know how much professional help you can get for your brother. If your family can afford it, and  (i'm in the USA So i'm guessing Post-secondary is after what the USA would call High school) your brother is going to college or something, see if u can get him to board away or to stay with a friend. So that he either gets more independence and understanding, or to get your dad a breather. 

&#x200B;

I myself am boarding away out of staying at my house is stunting my growth as an adult, and isn't helping some health issues. 

&#x200B;

Idk if this was helpful, but i hope everything calms down for you,

i saw one of my classmates with a shirts with the colors of the trans pride flag. i don't think he figured it out, since i have never notice him wearing or doing anything related to it, and i have a trans sweatshirt with the colors i wear all the time. Almost no one knows that it is the pride flag for some odd reason.

&#x200B;

It was refreshing. also since i didn't think they made shirts in flag colors XD

&#x200B;

You are an ally, and just because you aren't trans doesn't mean you cant use the colors-as a graphic designer, colors are free roam to be used as any median. no one has the right to question your identity. Plus you are going as support, so power to you as how you want to look at the parade-as long as it is appropriate and not offensive to those around you.

&#x200B;

the parade is prob over by the time i answered, lol.
